---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Disclosure from '../../components/Disclosure.astro';
import EmailCapture from '../../components/EmailCapture.astro';
import { url } from '../../utils/url';
import { SITE } from '../../consts';
import { goHref, retailerName } from '../../data/affiliate-config';
import tkData from '../../data/testkits.json';

interface Kit {
  brand: string; parameter: string; model: string; priceUSD: number;
  accuracy: string | null; resolution: string | null; range: string;
  testsPerKit: number; reagentRefillPriceUSD: number | null; reagentRefillTests?: number; refillSource?: string; testCountNote?: string;
  method: string; knownIssues?: string[]; retailers?: string[];
  source: string; priceSource: string; imageUrl?: string | null;
}
const data = tkData as any;
const kits = data.kits as Kit[];
const dataDate = data.generated as string;

const PARAMS = [
  { key: 'alkalinity', label: 'Alkalinity', note: 'Track closely when setting or changing a dosing schedule; adjust frequency to measured consumption.' },
  { key: 'calcium', label: 'Calcium', note: 'Test alongside alkalinity when setting a dosing schedule.' },
  { key: 'magnesium', label: 'Magnesium', note: 'Check when assessing the balance of calcium and alkalinity.' },
  { key: 'phosphate', label: 'Phosphate', note: 'The algae budget. Low numbers need real resolution to be meaningful.' },
  { key: 'nitrate', label: 'Nitrate', note: 'The other nutrient — modern reefs run it low but not zero.' },
];

const slug = (k: { brand: string; parameter: string }) =>
  `${k.brand}-${k.parameter}`.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-');
const money = (n: number) => `$${n.toLocaleString('en-US', { minimumFractionDigits: 2, maximumFractionDigits: 2 })}`;
const buy = (k: Kit) => goHref(k.retailers || [], `${k.brand} ${k.model} test kit`, k.priceSource);
const forParam = (p: string) => kits.filter((k) => k.parameter === p);

const pageURL = new URL(url('/reviews/best-reef-test-kits'), SITE.url).href;
const itemListLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'ItemList',
  name: 'Best Reef Test Kits — Hanna vs Salifert vs Red Sea',
  numberOfItems: kits.length,
  itemListElement: kits.map((k, i) => ({ '@type': 'ListItem', position: i + 1, name: `${k.brand} ${k.model}`, url: `${pageURL}#${slug(k)}` })),
};
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Which parameter should I test most often?',
    a: `Alkalinity is useful to track closely when you set up or change dosing. Test often enough to measure consumption and catch a change, then choose a schedule based on your tank. A fixed weekly schedule may miss a problem in a high-consumption reef.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Digital (Hanna) or titration (Salifert / Red Sea)?',
    a: `Hanna colorimeters use an optical reading; visual kits ask you to judge a color or titration endpoint. Both depend on correct sampling, clean vials, and the stated procedure. Compare the published range and accuracy for the exact model. Buy the instrument once, then compare reagent costs separately.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Why do two kits disagree on the same water?',
    a: `First check the units, sample volume, reagent expiry, and instructions for each kit. Do not multiply a Salifert phosphate result by a phosphorus conversion factor just because another instrument is used. A phosphate reading and a phosphorus reading are different units; only convert when the specific instructions require it. Repeat an unexpected reading before changing dosing.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Do ICP tests replace test kits?',
    a: `No. A lab report covers the tests listed by that lab; it does not provide live monitoring between samples. Check the actual analytes and turnaround before ordering. Keep an at-home testing plan that matches your tank and dosing routine.`,
  },
];
const faqLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })),
};

const headline = "Hanna vs Salifert vs Red Sea — the test kit face-off, by published specs";
---
<Base
  headline={headline}
  title="Best Reef Test Kits: Hanna, Salifert & Red Sea"
  description="Compare Hanna, Salifert, and Red Sea reef test kits by published accuracy, resolution, and cost per test for five common water parameters."
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Reviews', href: '/reviews' }, { name: 'Best Reef Test Kits', href: '/reviews/best-reef-test-kits' }]}
>
  <section class="container tool-wrap prose">
    <p class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--brand-2)">Reviews · Test Kits</p>
    <h1>{headline}</h1>
    <p class="lede-dark">Choose a test that covers the water level you need to measure, then compare its stated accuracy, resolution, and running cost. A reusable colorimeter has an upfront instrument cost plus later reagents; a visual kit bundles its supplies. The table keeps those costs separate.</p>
    <Disclosure />
    <p class="rnote" style="margin-top:0">Original kit specifications and prices are recorded from {dataDate}. Hanna refill prices and 25-test refill counts, plus Salifert specification links, were checked on October 25, 2026; no other kit price is described as refreshed. Each row links its specification and price sources. A missing accuracy value means it was not recorded in this dataset. <a href={url('/how-we-rate')}>Full methodology →</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="container" style="padding-top:8px;">
    <h2>The one-paragraph verdict</h2>
    <p style="max-width:68ch;">For <strong>alkalinity</strong>, choose between a digital readout and a visual titration based on the range, procedure, and costs you can sustain. Hanna's HI772 has a recorded {money(kits.find((k) => k.model.startsWith('HI772'))!.priceUSD)} instrument price; its verified {money(kits.find((k) => k.model.startsWith('HI772'))!.reagentRefillPriceUSD!)} refill supplies 25 tests, or {money(kits.find((k) => k.model.startsWith('HI772'))!.reagentRefillPriceUSD! / 25)} per later test. The instrument price divided by its starter tests is <em>not</em> the ongoing reagent cost. For other parameters, compare the actual row before choosing a brand.</p>

    {PARAMS.map((p) => (
      <>
        <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">{p.label}</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--muted);max-width:68ch;">{p.note}</p>
        <div class="tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={`${p.label} equipment comparison, scroll for all columns`}>
          <table class="specs">
            <thead><tr><th>Kit</th><th>Published accuracy</th><th>Resolution</th><th>Method</th><th>First-kit $/test</th><th>Refill $/test</th><th>Kit / instrument price</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              {forParam(p.key).map((k) => (
                <tr id={slug(k)}>
                  <td><strong>{k.brand}</strong> {k.model}<br /><a href={k.source} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Published specifications</a><br /><span style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.85em;">{k.testsPerKit} reference tests</span>{k.testCountNote && <><br /><small>{k.testCountNote}</small></>}</td>
                  <td>{k.accuracy || <em style="color:var(--muted)">not published</em>}</td>
                  <td>{k.resolution || <em style="color:var(--muted)">not published</em>}</td>
                  <td style="color:var(--muted)">{k.method}</td>
                  <td>{k.testsPerKit > 0 ? <strong>{money(k.priceUSD / k.testsPerKit)}</strong> : 'Not recorded'}<br /><small>Includes initial purchase</small></td>
                  <td>{k.reagentRefillPriceUSD != null && k.reagentRefillTests ? <><strong>{money(k.reagentRefillPriceUSD / k.reagentRefillTests)}</strong><br /><small>{money(k.reagentRefillPriceUSD)} / {k.reagentRefillTests} tests</small><br /><a href={k.refillSource} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Refill source</a></> : 'Refill count not verified'}</td>
                  <td><a class="aff aff-sm" href={buy(k)} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener">{money(k.priceUSD)} (paid link) ↗</a></td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </>
    ))}
    <p class="rnote">First-kit cost per test = initial kit or instrument price ÷ included test count. Refill cost per test = refill price ÷ the refill's own verified test count. Shipping, tax, wasted tests, expired reagents, and replacement hardware are excluded. Refills are shown only where their count was verified; a starter kit count is never assumed to be the refill count. Resolution describes the reading steps, not an accuracy guarantee.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="container prose" style="padding-top:24px;">
    <h2>Check the units before changing the tank</h2>
    <p>Salifert describes its test as measuring <a href="https://www.salifert.com/pt/po.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">phosphate</a>. Follow the chart and instructions supplied with your kit; do not automatically multiply a phosphate result by a phosphorus conversion factor. Phosphate and phosphorus are different reported quantities. Also check whether a result is in ppm or ppb.</p>
    <p>Use the exact sample volume, clean the vial, and check reagent dates. A digital display does not remove technique errors. Repeat an unexpected result before making a dosing change, and compare like units if you cross-check with another kit.</p>

    <h2>FAQ</h2>
    {faqs.map((f) => (
      <>
        <h3 style="font-size:1.05rem;">{f.q}</h3>
        <p style="color:var(--muted)">{f.a}</p>
      </>
    ))}
    <p>Reading high nitrate or phosphate? <a href={url('/tools/water-change-calculator')}>The water change calculator</a> turns the number into a plan, and <a href={url('/guides/carbon-dosing')}>the carbon dosing guide</a> covers export when dilution isn't enough. Dosing to targets: <a href={url('/tools/reef-dosing-calculator')}>the dosing calculator</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <EmailCapture />
  </section>

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(itemListLd)} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqLd)} />
</Base>

<style>
  .tablewrap { overflow-x: auto; background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
  table.specs { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .92rem; min-width: 720px; }
  table.specs th { text-align: left; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: .78rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; color: var(--muted); padding: 12px 14px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--line); }
  table.specs td { padding: 10px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; }
  table.specs tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
  .aff-sm { padding: 7px 12px; font-size: .8rem; }
</style>
